<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  DebugInspector advertises its HTTP server over Bonjour so iOS prompts for the
	  Local Network permission on first launch. Without this key in Info.plist the
	  prompt never appears and iOS silently drops LAN traffic to/from the app.
	  The rest of Info.plist is auto-generated from INFOPLIST_KEY_* build settings;
	  Xcode merges that generated content onto this base file.
	-->
	<key>NSBonjourServices</key>
	<array>
		<string>_primitive-inspector._tcp</string>
	</array>
	<!--
	  This app's own URL scheme, under the CFBundleURLName PrimitiveAuth that
	  PrimitiveAuthManager reads its callback scheme from. `primitive init`
	  stamps an app-unique scheme in place of `primitiveapp` — every app
	  scaffolded from this template would otherwise register the same one, and
	  iOS picks arbitrarily between two apps claiming a scheme.

	  Sign-in email: CODE-ONLY BY DEFAULT, and that works with no configuration
	  at all — the manager sends no redirect target, so the server never
	  consults the allow-list.

	  IF THIS APP HAS A WEB COUNTERPART, prefer the https link over the custom
	  scheme below: add "webUrl": "https://your-web-domain" to the environment
	  in .primitive/config.json (a bare origin; `primitive env add` takes a
	  web-url option when it CREATES an environment, but cannot edit one that
	  already exists) and the sign-in email carries
	  "https://your-web-domain/oauth/callback" instead. That one link
	  opens THIS app when it is installed (a universal link, once the domain
	  serves apple-app-site-association and the applinks entitlement names it)
	  and is an ordinary web sign-in in any browser. Allow-list that https URL
	  the same way. The full checklist is in the authentication guide.

	  Turning the custom-scheme LINK on instead takes two steps:

	    1. Merge "<scheme>://auth/magic-link" into the existing
	       [auth].emailRedirectUris array in your app's config/app.toml and
	       push the app settings with `primitive config push` (its option flag
	       spells a double hyphen, which an XML comment cannot contain — the
	       exact command is in the authentication guide).
	    2. Set `authManager.sendsEmailSignInLink = true` before sign-in.

	  What each missing piece looks like, so a half-wired app is diagnosable:
	    - flag on, URI not allow-listed  → EVERY email request fails 400
	                                       `Invalid redirect URI`
	    - allow-listed, scheme not here  → the emailed link is a dead tap;
	                                       nothing launches, nothing logs
	    - registered, nothing routing it → the app opens and no one signs in
	                                       (ContentView's .onOpenURL →
	                                       routePlatformLink does the routing)

	  A custom-scheme link only opens on a device that has this app installed:
	  dead in the Simulator, dead cross-device, and most webmail clients will
	  not render a non-http(s) href as a link — which is exactly what the https
	  link above fixes. The code is the credential that always works. The same
	  scheme carries the OAuth callback ("<scheme>://oauth/callback") when you
	  use `startOAuth()`.
	-->
	<key>CFBundleURLTypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>CFBundleURLName</key>
			<string>PrimitiveAuth</string>
			<key>CFBundleURLSchemes</key>
			<array>
				<string>primitiveapp</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
